   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I feel good with you.' The first content word means 'good', and 'you' rounds out the thought.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Мне тоже хорошо.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I feel good too.' Notice the word order: 'to me' comes first, and 'good' finishes the sentence.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Особенно когда ты без одежды.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Especially when you are without clothes.' In Russian, 'especially' leads into 'clothes' in a very natural everyday phrasing.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "max",
   "t": "Ты очень смешная.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You are very funny.' You'll hear 'you' all the time in the show, here connected with 'funny'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Я серьезно.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I am serious.' The key word here means 'I', which Sasha combines with 'seriously'. Then Max replies.",
